-- title:
--   Fricke and Atkin–Lehner involutions of the degeneracy roof
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $p$, let $N\ge 1$ with $p\nmid N$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\neq p$. Inside the Laurent series field over $\kappa$ write $\tilde\jmath=$ `jqModC κ`, the product of $q^{-1}$ with the power series `jNum` $=E_4^3\cdot$`dedekindEtaUnitInv` reduced into $\kappa$, and $\tilde\jmath_m=$ `jqNModC κ m`, its image under the substitution $q\mapsto q^m$ given by `qExpand κ m`; let $\overline F_N=$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` be the $\kappa$-subfield generated by $\{\tilde\jmath,\tilde\jmath_N\}$ and $R=$ `charLDegeneracyRoof κ N ℓ` the $\kappa$-subfield generated by $\{\tilde\jmath,\tilde\jmath_N,\tilde\jmath_\ell,\tilde\jmath_{N\ell}\}$, with $\alpha=$ `heckeAlphaC` the inclusion $\overline F_N\hookrightarrow R$ and $\beta=$ `heckeBetaC` the $\kappa$-algebra map $\overline F_N\to R$ induced by $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$. The assertion is threefold: (i) there is a $\kappa$-algebra automorphism $w$ of $\overline F_N$ with $w(\tilde\jmath)=\tilde\jmath_N$ and $w(\tilde\jmath_N)=\tilde\jmath$; (ii) for every $\kappa$-algebra automorphism $w$ of $\overline F_N$ satisfying those two equations there is a $\kappa$-algebra automorphism $w'$ of $R$ with $w'(\alpha x)=\beta(w x)$ and $w'(\beta x)=\alpha(w x)$ for all $x\in\overline F_N$; (iii) if in addition $\ell\nmid N$, there is a $\kappa$-algebra automorphism $w''$ of $R$ with $w''(\alpha x)=\beta x$ and $w''(\beta x)=\alpha x$ for all $x$.
--
--   These are the Fricke involution $w_N$ on the special fibre of the modular curve $X_0(N)$ and, on the degeneracy roof at $\ell$ (the function field of $X_0(N\ell)$ when $p\nmid N\ell$), the involutions $w_{N\ell}$ and, for $\ell\nmid N$, the partial Atkin–Lehner involution $w_\ell$, expressed as swap relations between the two degeneracy embeddings $\alpha,\beta$. The statement is used to transport Hecke data across the two degeneracy maps: for the row-sum and adjoint-pair relations attached to a supersingular level datum, for the permutation of supersingular places interchanging the two correspondences, and for the rank bound on the Hecke torsion quotient.
